# No new PHP development

- All new product work is ASP.NET Core only (`aspnet/src/EcomAE.Platform`).
- Do not add new `.php` files. Existing PHP stays on disk until `readyToRemovePhp=true`.
- Do not invent PHP decommission, broad nginx cutover, or PHP-primary restore.
- Production ERP / CP / BOS / storefront UI must not display the words `PHP`, `classic`, or `classical`, and must not link `/php-reference/*` or “classic ERP / classical CP”.
- Gated deploy runs `scripts/forbid_php_stack_leak.py` and refuses publish on leak or new PHP.
- Tests: `TenantUiStackDisclosureTests`, `NewPhpDevelopmentBlockedTests`.
- Do not raise the frozen PHP file count or rewrite the allowlist to sneak in new PHP.
